 - **Memory Complexity:** Increases with the number of boxes due to replicated storage at box borders for interpolation [S1].
 - **Performance:** Improves rendering speed by skipping invisible sub-volumes and reducing unnecessary lighting computations on zero-gradient voxels [S1].
-- **Strengths:** Effective for lit rendering by isolating surface voxels; adaptive to volume properties.
-- **Limitations:** Overhead increases with the number of boxes; minimal size restrictions may lead to inefficient "other" boxes.
-- **When to Use:** When lit rendering performance is critical and the volume has distinct surface and interior regions.
-- **When Not to Use:** When the overhead of managing many small boxes outweighs the benefits, or for unilluminated rendering where uniform boxes alone may suffice.
